<!-- FAQ -->
<section class="sec" id="faq" aria-label="Frequently asked questions">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="slbl rv" style="text-align:center">Got Questions</p>
    <h2 class="sh2 rv" style="text-align:center;margin-bottom:8px">We Have Straight Answers</h2>
    <p class="ssub rv" style="text-align:center;margin:0 auto 48px">No runaround, no jargon. Here's what most people want to know before they reach out.</p>
    <div class="faq-list rv">
      <div class="faq-item"><button class="faq-q" aria-expanded="false" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">How fast can you really buy my house in DFW?<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M10 3a.75.75 0 01.75.75v10.638l3.96-4.158a.75.75 0 111.08 1.04l-5.25 5.5a.75.75 0 01-1.08 0l-5.25-5.5a.75.75 0 111.08-1.04l3.96 4.158V3.75A.75.75 0 0110 3z" clip-rule="evenodd"/></svg></button><div class="faq-a">We can close in as little as 7 days anywhere in the DFW metroplex. In most cases we provide a cash offer within 24 hours of seeing your property. If you need more time — 30, 60, even 90 days — we work completely around your schedule.</div></div>
      <div class="faq-item"><button class="faq-q" aria-expanded="false" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">Do I need to clean out or repair the house first?<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M10 3a.75.75 0 01.75.75v10.638l3.96-4.158a.75.75 0 111.08 1.04l-5.25 5.5a.75.75 0 01-1.08 0l-5.25-5.5a.75.75 0 111.08-1.04l3.96 4.158V3.75A.75.75 0 0110 3z" clip-rule="evenodd"/></svg></button><div class="faq-a">Absolutely not. We buy houses completely as-is. Don't clean, don't repair, don't even take out the trash if you don't want to. Leave behind whatever you don't want to deal with — we handle everything after closing.</div></div>
      <div class="faq-item"><button class="faq-q" aria-expanded="false" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">Are there any fees, commissions, or hidden costs?<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M10 3a.75.75 0 01.75.75v10.638l3.96-4.158a.75.75 0 111.08 1.04l-5.25 5.5a.75.75 0 01-1.08 0l-5.25-5.5a.75.75 0 111.08-1.04l3.96 4.158V3.75A.75.75 0 0110 3z" clip-rule="evenodd"/></svg></button><div class="faq-a">Zero. No agent commissions, no transaction fees, no closing costs on your end — we cover all of that. The cash offer we make you is the exact amount you receive at closing. No deductions, no surprises.</div></div>
      <div class="faq-item"><button class="faq-q" aria-expanded="false" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">Can you help if I'm facing foreclosure in Dallas or Fort Worth?<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M10 3a.75.75 0 01.75.75v10.638l3.96-4.158a.75.75 0 111.08 1.04l-5.25 5.5a.75.75 0 01-1.08 0l-5.25-5.5a.75.75 0 111.08-1.04l3.96 4.158V3.75A.75.75 0 0110 3z" clip-rule="evenodd"/></svg></button><div class="faq-a">Yes. Foreclosure situations are something we navigate regularly. A fast cash sale can stop the process, preserve your credit from a seven-year hit, and potentially put money in your pocket rather than losing the home entirely. Reach out as soon as possible — timeline matters.</div></div>
      <div class="faq-item"><button class="faq-q" aria-expanded="false" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">My house has back taxes or liens — can you still buy it?<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M10 3a.75.75 0 01.75.75v10.638l3.96-4.158a.75.75 0 111.08 1.04l-5.25 5.5a.75.75 0 01-1.08 0l-5.25-5.5a.75.75 0 111.08-1.04l3.96 4.158V3.75A.75.75 0 0110 3z" clip-rule="evenodd"/></svg></button><div class="faq-a">Yes. Tax liens, back taxes, judgment liens, and code violations are things we deal with regularly. In many cases these can be resolved directly from the sale proceeds at closing — you don't need to come up with money upfront.</div></div>
      <div class="faq-item"><button class="faq-q" aria-expanded="false" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">How do you determine your cash offer?<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M10 3a.75.75 0 01.75.75v10.638l3.96-4.158a.75.75 0 111.08 1.04l-5.25 5.5a.75.75 0 01-1.08 0l-5.25-5.5a.75.75 0 111.08-1.04l3.96 4.158V3.75A.75.75 0 0110 3z" clip-rule="evenodd"/></svg></button><div class="faq-a">Our offer is based on the current market value of your property in its present condition — factoring in comparable sales in your neighborhood, location, and what repairs the home may need. We are fully transparent about how we arrive at our number and never pressure anyone to accept.</div></div>
      <div class="faq-item"><button class="faq-q" aria-expanded="false" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">Is this legitimate? How am I protected?<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M10 3a.75.75 0 01.75.75v10.638l3.96-4.158a.75.75 0 111.08 1.04l-5.25 5.5a.75.75 0 01-1.08 0l-5.25-5.5a.75.75 0 111.08-1.04l3.96 4.158V3.75A.75.75 0 0110 3z" clip-rule="evenodd"/></svg></button><div class="faq-a">Every transaction closes through a licensed Texas title company — the same way any conventional home sale works. You never hand over keys or sign documents directly to us without full title company protection. The title company verifies the transaction and handles all fund disbursement.</div></div>
      <div class="faq-item"><button class="faq-q" aria-expanded="false" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">What if I owe more than the house is worth?<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M10 3a.75.75 0 01.75.75v10.638l3.96-4.158a.75.75 0 111.08 1.04l-5.25 5.5a.75.75 0 01-1.08 0l-5.25-5.5a.75.75 0 111.08-1.04l3.96 4.158V3.75A.75.75 0 0110 3z" clip-rule="evenodd"/></svg></button><div class="faq-a">This is an underwater or upside-down property, and it's a situation we can often still help with. In some cases a short sale may be an option. It's worth a conversation — even in difficult equity situations there may be a path forward that beats the alternatives.</div></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

</main>

